  "summary": "Malicious code in lucy-python-script-2030 (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (2195ea343abdb1205451fc7c778bdd1580cf985461949081852e9e82363ac389)\nThe package was found to contain malicious code or consuming dependency that contains malicious code\n\n## Source: kam193 (0b93ebb2207ccfa0d02d068d444dce91835203dfe89a5ece38906158b4d3b891)\nStarting version 0.1.1, the package contains an infostealer attempting to exfiltrate during import various sensitive data, like browser data, sensitive files, cloud credentials and others. In analyzed versions, the code contained mistakes effectievly disarming the functionality.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-09-lucy-python-script-2030\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - infostealer\n\n\n - exfiltration-browser-data\n\n\n - files-exfiltration\n\n\n - persistence\n\n\n - The package contains code to detect if it is running in a sandbox environment.\n\n\n - uses-telegram-bot\n\n\n - exfiltration-cloud-tokens\n",
